<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Offered sizes: 1x1 and 2x1 (2 wide, 1 tall) on every launcher, plus
     1x2 and 2x2 on launchers with a row pitch under 80dp (e.g. the Samsung
     S26 Ultra's One UI launcher, where a 2-row placement is the launcher's
     native short-row cell). Offer matrix (pitch = the launcher's grid
     pitch; column range = ceil(minWidth/pitch)..floor-style max from
     maxWidth, row range = ceil(minHeight/pitch)..ceil(maxHeight/pitch)):
     - WIDTH 40..190dp: 1 column on every launcher with a ≥40dp column
       pitch (40dp is the smallest pitch the AOSP widget picker grid uses,
       the same AOSP-safe floor as before — the Pixel 7 Pro's picker pitch
       is in [40, 80) dp, so the old 80dp minimum hid the 1-column tile);
       2 columns whenever 190dp ≥ 1.5× the pitch (a 484 dp-wide screen's
       ≈121 dp cell — the Pixel — and the ≈89-95 dp cells of the A52 and
       S26-class grids all qualify) → 1-2 columns.
     - HEIGHT 40..80dp: min = 40dp keeps the 1-row minimum on every
       launcher (ceil(40/pitch) = 1 for pitch ≥ 40dp) — including
       launchers whose row pitch is shorter than the old 80dp floor (the
       One UI / S26 Ultra case: its pitch is under 80 dp, so the old 80dp
       floor forced a 2-row minimum and, with the max also 80dp, locked
       the range at two rows — the picker offered only 1x2). max = 80dp
       offers 1-2 rows on short-row launchers (ceil(80/pitch) = 2 for
       pitch < 80dp → 1x2/2x2 become placeable there) and exactly 1 row
       on tall-row launchers (ceil(80/pitch) = 1 for pitch ≥ 80dp — the
       Pixel ≈116 dp, the A52 ≈89 dp — so their offer stays 1x1 + 2x1).
     - targetCell 1x1: the default placement size.
     - resizeMode horizontal|vertical: the widget may be stretched across
       columns AND down a row; the actual offer per launcher is capped by
       the min/max ranges above (1-2 x 1 on tall-row launchers, 1-2 x
       1-2 on short-row launchers).
     - Content fit per size (pinned in WidgetContent.kt): the budget is the
       tightest of the host-reported candidate allocations — API 31+
       launchers push them into the stable widget options
       (OPTION_APPWIDGET_SIZES, a list of px sizes; the app re-renders on
       onAppWidgetOptionsChanged), so the span-agnostic fit is correct at
       whatever size any launcher offers. Hosts
       that don't report an allocation (pre-API 31, or a host that never
       pushes sizes) fall back to the 89dp default budget. The render is
       span-agnostic (the widget cannot read its own span from the stable
       options API), so every layout is pinned to the tightest 1x1 cell:
       * 1-row cell: the full layout (worst case 82dp) is kept whenever the
         allocation holds it — every host that doesn't report an allocation
         (A52 ≈89dp, Pixel ≈116dp, unknown) and every reporting host whose
         1-row cell is ≥82dp; a sub-80dp allocation — the documented
         Samsung S26 Ultra One UI short row (pitch under 80dp, pinned
         conservatively against the 64dp tight case) — renders compact
         (the secondary freshness line dropped; at the pinned 64dp the
         render is at most 62dp — 3 rows without the freshness line — or
         60dp with the "+N more" line), and even tighter allocations drop
         grid rows into the "+N more" count until the remainder fits.
       * 2-row cell (short-row launchers only): the allocation is
         2×pitch ≥ 2×40dp = 80dp (the 40dp minResize floor), so the fit
         rules yield the full layout when the allocation is ≥82dp or the
         72dp compact worst case when it is 80-81dp — it always fits.
     - min/maxResize (API 31+) agree with the min/max offer ranges;
       launchers below API 31 ignore these attributes and fall back to
       the resizeMode behaviour. -->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:minWidth="40dp"
    android:minHeight="40dp"
    android:minResizeWidth="40dp"
    android:minResizeHeight="40dp"
    android:maxResizeWidth="190dp"
    android:maxResizeHeight="80dp"
    android:maxWidth="190dp"
    android:maxHeight="80dp"
    android:targetCellWidth="1"
    android:targetCellHeight="1"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="1800000"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/widget_preview"
    android:previewLayout="@layout/widget_preview"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen"
    android:description="@string/widget_description" />
